<li class="gl rv"><span class="k">neatlogs measured</span><b>64 runs, one cost spread</b><p>Mean $0.0167 a run. One run in twenty costs $0.0508, and the worst cost $0.1014.</p><a href="https://github.com/HighnessAtharva/firstrun/blob/main/business/drivers.csv">drivers.csv, with a trace per row</a></li>
<li class="gl rv"><span class="k">cfo.ai modeled</span><b>18 months from the traces</b><p>Ari built three plans, Stripe fees, churn and six Scenarios. Every cost cell reads the measured drivers.</p><a href="https://cfo.ai/s/_u5lbrHIl9KX_JQE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the public model</a></li>
<li class="gl rv hot"><span class="k">The plan found</span><b>Cash runs out in month 14</b><p>The agent capped a run at $0.50, so a Scale run could cost five times its $0.0997 share of the fee.</p><a href="https://github.com/HighnessAtharva/firstrun/blob/main/business/BUSINESS_PLAN.md">Read the business plan</a></li>
<li class="gl rv"><span class="k">FirstRun fixed</span><b>The plan sets the cap</b><p><code>firstrun run --tier scale</code> stops a run at $0.028. A live Free-tier run stopped at $0.0115 of its $0.0108 cap.</p><a href="https://github.com/HighnessAtharva/firstrun/pull/15">See the change, PR #15</a></li>
